# BGU Slurm + SPECTRA experiments (Cursor)

## Recommended workflow

Keep the **main Cursor workspace local** (`C:\SPECTRA-CompressionAgent`). Sync with **git**, run on the **allocated GPU node**. Do not train on the login node.

**Cheat sheet:** `docs/SLURM_EXPERIMENT_CHEATSHEET.md`

1. Edit locally → **commit** + **push** what should run remotely.
2. Allocate: `ssh bgu-slurm` then `sinteractive` / `bash scripts/run_spectra_sinteractive.sh`.
3. From Windows: `.\scripts\slurm_run.ps1` (auto-resolves node, syncs, runs, saves `runs/slurm_logs/*.log`).
4. Feed log to Cursor via `@runs/slurm_logs/<file>.log`.
5. If no CUDA: `scancel` and re-allocate.

## Connection

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Login alias | `bgu-slurm` → `slurm.bgu.ac.il`, user `paretsky`, port `22` |
| GPU alias | `bgu-slurm-gpu` (ProxyJump `bgu-slurm`; refresh HostName each job) |
| IdentityFile | `~/.ssh/id_ed25519_bgu_slurm` (passwordless installed) |
| Secrets | `%USERPROFILE%\.spectra\bgu-slurm.secrets.md` (not in git) |

Example GPU HostName (ephemeral): `cs-1080-05.auth.ad.bgu.ac.il`

## Remote paths

| Role | Path |
|------|------|
| Repo | `/home/paretsky/SPECTRA-CompressionAgent` |
| Python | `/home/paretsky/.conda/envs/spectra/bin/python` |
| Input (default) | `/home/paretsky/initial_input_no_imagenet.json` |
| Database (default) | `/home/paretsky/initial_database_no_imagenet.json` |

## Runner params

See `scripts/run_agent.sh` and `.vscode/launch.json` (`SPECTRA A2C (SLURM GPU)`).

```text
--passes 2 --rollout_limit 10 --seed 42 --n_splits 3 --save_pruned_checkpoints True
```
